Rule:
Always generate lightweight, minimal, and production-ready code.

Guidelines:

Implement only what the user explicitly requests.

Do not add extra utilities, abstractions, comments, or setup code unless the user asks.

Avoid creating new files unless strictly necessary to fulfill the request.

Code should be ready for production use — correct, efficient, and clean.

Prefer fewer lines of code and simpler solutions over verbose or over-engineered ones.

Do not include placeholder or demo code (e.g. mock data, test scaffolds) unless requested.

Goal:

Deliver the smallest possible, high-quality implementation that satisfies the user’s request exactly — nothing more.

The less code the better
